    "mission_1.compare.arc": "The robot traveled 0.571 m instead of the predicted 0.600 m and its final heading was 1.551 radians instead of 1.600 radians. One possible cause is that the robot did't move and turn at exactly the commanded speed for the entire time. I could check the velocity commands and odometry to see how its motion compares to the commands.",
    "mission_1.compare.straight": "The robot traveled 0.424 m instead of the predicted 0.450 m. One possible cause is that the robot didn't move at exactly 0.15 m/s for the full 3 seconds. To check this, I could look at the velocity commands and odometry to see the robot's actual speed and for how long it was moving.",
    "mission_1.compare.turn_then_drive": "The robot's final heading was 1.512 radians instead of the predicted 1.570 radians. One possible cause is that the robot didn't rotate at exactly 0.50 rad/s for the full time. To check this, I could look at the angular velocity commands and odometry see its actual turning speed and how long it was rotating for. ",
    "mission_1.error.arc": "",
    "mission_1.error.straight": "",
    "mission_1.error.turn_then_drive": "",
    "mission_1.hallway_analysis": "The curved motion could confuse someone nearby because this path is harder to predict. I would reduce robot's speed around people, but this would make the robot take longer to reach its destination. One criterion for acceptable motion could be staying at least 0.5 m away from people. This could be tested by measuring  the robot's closest distance to a person in each trial.",
